# ChangeLog

## v0.97.0 (2026-07-13)

### User Features
- Run a program by name: `jnext game.tap` now works exactly like `--load game.tap`

### Developer Features
- Debugger video panel gains "All layers" (the composed picture) and "Background colour" views
- `--delayed-screenshot-layers` captures any subset of ULA / Layer 2 / sprites / tilemap
- The two ULA views now say which screen bank the ULA is actually reading
- Per-subsystem log levels, e.g. `--log-level cpu=trace,video=warn`

### Bug Fixes
- Stepping through a frame no longer corrupts the emulation: the Copper and every raster split were being wiped
- Debugger no longer reports Layer 2 disabled when a program enables it through port 0x123B
- Debugger's NextREG panel no longer disturbs the Pi-I2S sample the program is about to read
- Debugger video panels fixed: wrong memory bank, no per-scanline replay, and one panel corrupted live scroll state
- A screenshot that cannot be written is now an error with a non-zero exit, not a silent success

### Internal JNEXT Development
- Test suites are declared in config files with pinned row counts: a missing test is a loud failure, never a silent skip
- Two unit-test suites that had never once run now run — 63 assertions no count had ever included
- The test harness is itself under test: 26 self-test cases, run by every regression
- ccache wired into the build: a clean rebuild drops from 65 s to 9 s
- Test results no longer depend on the user's locale

## v0.96.0 (2026-07-12)

### Bug Fixes
- Constant noise/buzz throughout a session fixed — the audio device was starved and SDL filled the gaps with silence (issue #7)
- Clicking over beeper music fixed; worst on machines with little CPU headroom, which is why issue #7 was reported as a constant hum
- Beeper music no longer has a high-pitched tone over it: the mixer is sampled by integration instead of point-sampling (aliasing)
- Emulation now paces on the sound card's clock, so audio never drifts ahead of or behind the emulator

### Internal JNEXT Development
- Reverted the v0.95.x DC-blocking mixer stage: it never fixed issue #7, it masked it, and it distorted beeper waveforms
- New audio-underrun regression test captures jnext's real audio output and fails if silence is ever spliced into the stream

## v0.95.0 (2026-07-11)

### User Features
- SD card is now optional: with no --sdcard, jnext finds, or offers to download and patch, the official NextZXOS image
- Download progress dialog while the distribution image is fetched
- SD-card flag renamed to --sdcard (the old --sd-card is still accepted)

### Developer Features
- --rtc pins the emulated real-time clock to a fixed date/time for deterministic boot screenshots
- --sdcard-download-confirm / --sdcard-download-force control the built-in image download

### Bug Fixes
- NextZXOS mid-boot colour-garbage glitch fixed (bank 5 is now dedicated VRAM, un-aliased from external SRAM)
- SD/SPI card responses conform to spec (2 idle bytes before R1, no $FF in CMD58 reply, real CRC-16 data checksums)
- Multiface memory window backed by external SRAM on the Next, matching hardware
- +3 machine-type register reports the VHDL cold-boot default

### Internal JNEXT Development
- Firmware-bypass route (--bypass-tbblue-fw) and its tooling removed now that native boot works
- Host-side SD-image formatting rebuilt on vendored ChaN FatFs; downloads via libcurl; SHA256 integrity guard on the cached image
- Boot-to-menu screenshot regressions added; unit tests 4232 pass / 0 fail, regression 46/0/0

## v0.94.0 (2026-07-10)

### User Features
- NextZXOS boots natively from the SD card image through the authentic FPGA boot chain (welcome screen + main menu)
- Instant TAP loading via phantom typist, plus FUSE-style fastload mode
- Pristine z88dk NEX games boot without patching via the esxDOS stub option
- Host hotkeys for hardware buttons: Multiface NMI, DivMMC NMI, soft and hard reset
- Per-scanline render-state replay (palette, sprites, tilemap, ULA) enables demo-class raster effects
- Mouse: host cursor hidden over the emulator window, position scaling fixed

### Developer Features
- CPU T-state profiler with per-physical-address counters and z88dk map-file heatmap script
- Headless automation: delayed keypress injection and compositor per-pixel trace dump
- Env-gated NextZXOS boot diagnostics (instruction trace ring, trap detector, boot probes)

### Bug Fixes
- Layer 2 320x256 mode no longer shows animated noise on the right half of the screen
- Inverted ULA attributes in Next mode fixed
- Kempston mouse Y axis now uses Cartesian convention
- Bank-7 memory no longer aliases the alt-ROM area (fixed NextZXOS workspace corruption)
- Standalone 128K/+3 machines keep bank 7 intact after Next machine switches
- SD card: open multi-block reads survive chip-select release; single card no longer answers both slots
- Builds cleanly on Debian 12 / GCC 12 from a fresh clone

### Internal JNEXT Development
- Full-subsystem VHDL-conformance audit waves with enumeration-table mandate; hundreds of fixes landed
- Unit-test SKIP-reduction: dashboard grew to 4116 cases at 99% pass, zero failures
- Screenshot regression suite expanded from 30 to 43 cases
- Symmetric-trace differential debugging against reference emulators (CSpect plugin, zx_go harness)
- Multiface core subsystem modelled and VHDL-verified
- Machine ID now reports real-hardware value; soft reset preserves the Z80 register file per VHDL

## v0.93.0

### Bug Fixes
- CTC channel chaining now uses ring topology (ch3→ch0) matching VHDL
- +3 ROM-high bit via port 0x1FFD now observable + NR 0x82 bit 3 gating
- Specdrum port 0xDF read handler for VHDL port_1f combo gate
- I2C ACK phase off-by-one — read data was shifted left by one bit

### Internal JNEXT Development
- Unit tests: 2556 pass, 0 fail, 696 skip (3252 total across 19 suites)
- Regression suite: 34/34 clean
- Uniform test output format across all 19 test suites
- Color-coded `make unit-test` target with per-suite totals
- Version bumping procedure documented in CLAUDE.md

## v0.92.0

### User Features
- 640px native framebuffer for tilemap 80-col and Layer 2 640x256 modes
- Floating bus emulation enabled for all machine types
- Compositor blend modes 110 (additive) and 111 (subtractive)
- Pentagon, Kempston joystick, mouse, and ULA+ ports now respond

### Developer Features
- Debugger: improved interrupt and tilemap split-screen debugging

### Bug Fixes
- Z80 instruction timing and contention fixes — games now run at correct speed
- NEX loader: palette, sprite, transparency, and init fixes
- Tilemap rendering, scrolling, control-bit swap, and 80-col pixel addressing
- Compositor NR 0x14 palette-compare transparency for ULA and Layer 2
- Port dispatch exclusive routing and VHDL-correct decode masks
- NR 0x82-0x85 port-enable register defaults and gating
- DivMMC mapram OR-latch, read_control mask, ROM3 automap gating
- DMA prescaler, ULA frame timing, AY envelope, SPI decode, MMU reset

### Internal JNEXT Development
- Subsystem compliance tests: 1150/1171 pass (98%)
- Regression suite: 34/34 clean
- 15 emulator fixes + 9 test reclassifications across 21 backlog items

## v0.91.0

### User Features
- ZX Spectrum 48K, 128K, +2A/+3, Pentagon, and Next machine types
- ULA, Layer 2 (256/320/640), Sprites (8-bit/4-bit), Tilemap, Copper
- 6-mode layer compositor with per-scanline border colour
- 8 palettes with 9-bit RGB (512 colours)
- AY/YM x3 TurboSound, 4-channel DAC, Beeper
- NEX, SNA, SZX, TAP, TZX, WAV, RZX file formats
- Qt 6 GUI: Hi-DPI, fullscreen, CRT filter, speed control, screenshots, MPEG4 video recording

### Developer Features
- Debugger: registers, disassembly, hex editor, breakpoints, trace, symbol tables
- Magic breakpoint (ED FF / DD 01) and magic debug port
- Headless mode for automated testing and screenshot regression suite
- Backwards execution: Step Back, Frame Back, rewind slider

### Bug Fixes
- (initial release)

### Internal JNEXT Development
- FUSE-based Z80 core with Z80N extensions (26 opcodes)
- Memory contention for 48K, 128K, +3, Pentagon timing models
- IM1/IM2 interrupt controller with 14 Next interrupt levels
- DivMMC with automap, CTC, UART, DMA, SPI, I2C/RTC peripherals
